No; Section 7(3) protects only persons 'against whom an offence was committed';
           voluntary proposers without antecedent demand or coercion cannot be characterised as
           aggrieved persons protected by the immunity.

No; civil liability turns on proprietary entitlement without requiring proof of mental
            state, whereas criminal liability independently requires established fraudulent intent;
            civil liability cannot supply the mens rea element in the criminal complaint.

Yes; Section 5 restricts judicial intervention to situations expressly provided in Part I;
           Section 16 enumerates no stage-based judicial challenge right, and the legislature's
           silence constitutes an implied exclusion of court review.
